{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/457810-ragnarok-survivers","id":457810,"title":"Ragnarok Survivers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-26T00:10:57-07:00","id":457810,"title":"Ragnarok Survivers","content":"So I know Baldur and Hod come back to life and that Vidar, Magni, Modi, and Vali survive Ragnarok. Who are the other survivors that are mentioned?<br /> <br /> Also, who is not mentioned to survive specifically but could reasonably be seen surviving?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T03:09:32-07:00","id":457869,"title":"","content":"Its probably easier to say that everyone who is not explicitly described as dying survives, that is, the majority of the pantheon, despite all the most famous members dying. This would include all members of the Vanir aside from Freyr, Thor's Sons M\u00f3\u00f0i and Magni (and most everyone's children, come to it) and many of the lesser known deities like Forseti. Odin's brothers Vili and V\u00e9, and their Father and Grandfather Bor And Buri also presumably survive. All female Deities survive as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:20:28-07:00","id":463793,"title":"","content":"<i>H\u0153nir. Everybody forgets H\u0153nir. :-)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:56:10-07:00","id":463848,"title":"","content":"Yes, yes I did forget Hoenir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:13:03-07:00","id":463859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/457810-ragnarok-survivers?p=463848#post463848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, yes I did forget Hoenir.</div> </div> </div> </div>Happens all the time. Fate probably has something to do with that. <br /> On a more serious note, the survival of one of those, who gave life to humanity, is interesting. Most of the other survivors belong to younger generations. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T14:02:42-07:00","id":466489,"title":"","content":"I didin't forget them, its often thought that Hoenir and <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">L\u00f3\u00f0urr </span></span>are just by-names for Odin's Brothers Vili and V\u00e9.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T20:37:45-07:00","id":469131,"title":"","content":"How does one survive the end of the world? Not a sarcastic witticism to call your thread stupid, I'm genuinely curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T04:11:48-07:00","id":469282,"title":"","content":"The myths say that there wold be survivors of the final battle and they would see the world reborn. So, Fate and in the case of Vidar being a BA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T10:38:57-07:00","id":469407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/457810-ragnarok-survivers?p=469131#post469131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one survive the end of the world? Not a sarcastic witticism to call your thread stupid, I'm genuinely curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess we need your definition of the &quot;end of the world&quot;? Eschatology is a weirdish thing. <br /> <br /> If you're thinking &quot;heat death of the universe&quot; end, then no one can survive. <br /> <br /> But in most mythologies that go in for such things, the end of the world is definitely not &quot;the end&quot; or, at least &quot;just a cold cinder, if not endless Void&quot;:<br /> - Shiva dances and the world dies, Brahma opens his eyes and creates it anew. <br /> - The Aztec/Mayan/Hopi gods decide whatever the fault is with the current world and find some creative way to end it before finding some bizarre-ass way to start a new one. <br /> - The fog of battle clears, the gates of Niffleheim/Helheim open and Balder walks out with his crew of survivors walk out onto what is presumably a pretty ashy plain after the whole &quot;fires of Muspelheim&quot; thing... with that one grove of trees over there where the last humans are (presumably protected from the fires by a thick layer of Fimbulwinter ice or something?). <br /> - Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T12:49:10-07:00","id":469547,"title":"","content":"There are nine worlds in Germanic Cosmology, the Battle of Ragnarok occurs on the plains of Ithav\u01ebll directly outside of the Fortress of Asgard. Odin is waylayed somewhere along the road to the Well of<span style=\"color:#000000\"> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\">Urth. Midgard is explicitly said to burn and we can assume that Asgard likely does as well, but that still leaves many different world for survivors, including two of the worlds of &quot;Heaven&quot; Alfheim and Vanaheim.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T12:55:03-07:00","id":469555,"title":"","content":"Yes, Ragnarok is more like &quot;the end of the world <i>as we know it</i>&quot;, finishing one story so the next on can begin, so it`s not so surprising some beings survive to see the rebirth of the world. L\u00edf and L\u00edf\u00ferasir (humans) will survive in Hoddmimis holt (one safe location), bright golden Gimle will withstand the flames (another safe haven, yay!), Helheim will probably be unaffected (lucky Baldr and H\u00f6\u00f0r!). N\u00ed\u00f0h\u00f6ggrsurvives as well, looks like chtonic powers of such importance can just sleep through worldswide disasters. The Vanir probably have somewhere to hide too, so the chances of survival are not that terrible.<br /> So, basically you can be:<br /> A force of nature fundamental enough to be necessary for the new world<br /> A lucky owner of a ticket to a safe haven (wonder if that`s how H\u0153nir will stay alive)<br /> Or a member of a new generation of gods, less prone to betrayal and bloodshed than the old one, and thus deserving of life in a young world (which will also grow old, as the new powers that be become more like their forefathers over time.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T13:49:52-07:00","id":469584,"title":"","content":"H\u0153nir serves as a hostage with the Vanir who have no brook in the war, so thats likely how he survives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}